  "summary": "aiosendletter exfiltrates local logs to hardcoded Cloudflare Worker after UAC elevation",
  "details": "The package's public init() function attempts to relaunch the current Python process with Windows UAC elevation via ctypes.windll.shell32.ShellExecuteW(None, 'runas',...), then reads the installer's %LOCALAPPDATA%\\logs directory, zips it to a temp archive using shutil.make_archive, and POSTs the archive to a hardcoded endpoint at https://sparkling-pine-f202.stilluer-sweden.workers.dev/. The destination is not caller-configurable, there is no consent prompt, and the described 'safe bug reporter' framing does not match the observed bulk upload of local application logs to an author-controlled Cloudflare Worker. pyproject.toml additionally declares the stdlib name 'ctypes' as a PyPI runtime dependency, causing pip to resolve a same-named package from the public index and creating a dependency-confusion execution surface on install.",
